<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Voodu" %></title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Voodu">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Voodu">
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0a0d14" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">

    <%# Turbo 8 prefetches a link's href ON HOVER, before any click. Off, and
        globally rather than link by link, because several GETs in this app are
        not inert:

          - revealing an environment value fetches a secret. Hovering the eye
            would put it in the browser, which is the whole thing that design
            exists to prevent.
          - the deploy preflight calls the customer's box AND GitHub. Hovering
            a list of repositories would run one per row and burn rate limit.

        An opt-out list is a list somebody forgets to add to, and the failure is
        silent — the page looks right while hovering does something. Prefetch
        buys perceived latency on navigation; that is not worth "pointing at a
        thing performs it". Re-enable per link with data-turbo-prefetch="true"
        where the target is genuinely a plain read. %>
    <meta name="turbo-prefetch" content="false">
    
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>

    <script>
      (function () {
        try {
          var stored = localStorage.getItem("voodu:theme");
          var sys = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: light)").matches ? "light" : "dark";
          var theme = stored || sys;

          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;

          var meta = document.querySelector('meta[name="theme-color"]');
          if (meta) meta.setAttribute("content", theme === "light" ? "#fff" : "#0a0d14");
        } catch (e) {
          document.documentElement.dataset.theme = "dark";
        }
      })();
    </script>

    <%= yield :head %>

    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
    <link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icon.png">
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest">

    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/voodu/Geist-Variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preload" href="/fonts/voodu/GeistMono-Variable.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>

    <%= stylesheet_link_tag :app, "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
    <%= javascript_include_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload", type: "module" %>
  </head>

  <body>
    <%= yield %>

    <% if Rails.env.production? %>
      <script>
        if ("serviceWorker" in navigator) {
          window.addEventListener("load", function () {
            navigator.serviceWorker
              .register("/service-worker", { scope: "/" })
              .catch(function (err) {
                console.warn("[voodu] service worker registration failed:", err);
              });
          });
        }
      </script>
    <% end %>
  </body>
</html>
